with a hilarious deleted post-credits  scene a surprise ending for camilo and  an even darker fate for abuela's husband  the ending of encanto was almost very  different yupikai movie lovers i'm jan  and in this video i'm revealing the  alternate endings for encanto you never  got to see spoilers ahead of course so  take care  during the beautiful melancholy song dos  uruguitas we get the full backstory of  abuela and her husband pedro how they  met fell in love got married had  triplets and then how he tragically died  trying to protect his family and the  town's people from a group of soldiers  however this scene was originally going  to be even more heartbreaking because in  early drafts alma and pedro had to flee  their town before the children were born  and according to encounter co-director  jared bush there was a version where she  had the babies at the river and they  were born the same moment pedro died now  pedro's fate was already pretty dark for  a disney movie but i think that alma  giving birth as their husband died  beside her would have been even more  bleak there is a tiny trace of this idea  in the final movie and the following  line which bush has confirmed does imply  that pedro died on the very day the  triplets were born when my three babies  had just been born urabuelo pedro and i  were forced to flee our home thankfully  they decided not to go with this  alternate ending meaning pedro did at  least get to say goodbye to his three  children before his death  bush also revealed that chispy the  capybara had a funny fully animated  post-credits scene that didn't make it  into the movie in the deleted scene  chispy lifts his leg to relieve himself  on the casita but the magical house  stops the little capybara by tipping a  drain full of water on him giving the  creature a taste of his own medicine  bush said the scene was cut because they  preferred to finish the movie on the  emotion and joy of the family coming  back together the mischievous casita can  also be seen pranking a capybara in this  unused concept art where it tips the  cute creature off a chair  in another alternate storyline mirabelle  had a confrontation with her mother  julieta at the end of the movie rather  than her grandmother as happened in the  final film in this version it was  mirabelle's anger with her mother that  led to the casita's destruction as with  each angry word she uttered it was as if  a blow was being struck to the house  causing it to break apart the idea was  that mirabel and casita shared a mental  connection so her rage would end up  wrecking the family home  in another version of the story the  casita was destroyed by fire burning to  the ground rather than crumbling to  pieces it would have been especially  poignant for a fire to destroy the  magical house given that it owed its  existence to a candle in the aftermath  of the fire the windows and doors  survived to give a sense of the original  layout of the home and a spooky  ghost-like shadow was also going to  appear this was supposed to feel like  there was a ghostly spirit still in the  ruins of the house a shadow that haunted  it perhaps that of abuela's pedro it was  meant to feel scary and threatening  although as the camera drew closer it  would be revealed to actually be the  remaining cracks of the house  a potentially confusing alternate ending  for camilo was considered at one time  where according to jared bush after the  house fell and the magic died camilo  reverted to his true self and no one  recognized him that ending would have  meant that the appearance we saw camilo  used throughout the movie when he wasn't  shape-shifting wasn't actually his real  form it was just another character he  was pretending to be i can see this  ending for camilo could have been  distracting given the number of  questions it would have raised and as  bush explained it was scrapped because  the moment had to be about mirabel  the casita also took on some creepy  ghost-like characteristics in this  unused concept art where the house  revealed there was something wrong by  having all the paintings and pictures go  blank the idea here was that the casita  was sick in a way and was experiencing  the kind of memory loss or brain fog  that people can get sometimes when  they're sick or suffering  another way to represent the magic going  wrong was this scene where the yellow  butterflies would have all gone dark  giving the moment a very spooky and  creepy vibe  and these unused pieces of concept art  show how in another version of the movie  the casita could literally float above  the ground both before it was destroyed  and later again when mirabel restores it  a deleted scene released by disney on  the encanto blu-ray appears to follow up  on the confrontation i mentioned earlier  between mirabel and her mother julieta  the cut scene takes place after a  devastated mirabelle has fled the  encounter filled with guilt and regret  for how she believes she's to blame for  the state of the family and alma decides  to go in search of her abuela sets out  on her own promising that when she  returns and julieta has healed they will  repair the family stronger than ever  after abuela arrives in her former  hometown she discovers a mural dedicated  to her beloved pedro with the words to  love us all is to love entirely and a  painting of him in the river with his  arms held up which honors the sacrifice  he made for the rest of the town when he  confronted the group of soldiers about  to attack them abuela wells up with  emotion at the memory of pedro and  remains at the mural overnight until the  following day a child tells her where  mirabelle is and in the alternate ending  abuela also confesses how after pedro's  death she held on too tight to her  family afraid to lose them again after i  lost him  i was so afraid i couldn't bear the  thought of losing anyone else and i  realize now  that my husband would be  so disappointed  because of all the people he would have  wished to understand his words it was me  and i am  so sorry a touch of this did make it  into the final film i was given a  miracle a second chance and i was so  afraid to lose it till i lost sight of  who or miracle was for and i am so sorry  there's also a fascinating alternate  reconciliation between mirabelle and  abuela hinted at in this concept art  where alma's hair transformed into a  river that ran for miles and mirabelle  had to find and follow the path of the  river in order to reach her grandmother  the idea here was to explore abuela's  ptsd following her husband's death and i  think the fantastically long river would  have been a metaphor for the depth of  alma's sorrow and how hard it was to  reach her emotionally the concept of  abuela's hair as a river fits nicely  with colombia's famous magical realism  which also inspired the rest of the  movie including the yellow butterflies  and magical rooms now if you'd love to  see even more deleted capybara moments  including them trash talking the maddie  girls be sure to subscribe and hit the  notification bell to get my next video  where i'll be talking about that and  more encounter deleted scenes i'll add a  link here and in the description as soon  as it's ready so what do you think of  these alternate endings and what would  you like to see happen in a future  encounter sequel or series let me know  in the comments below next tap left to  discover everything you missed at  encanto and if you enjoyed this video  then do leave a thumbs up i really  appreciate it thanks for enjoying this  movie with me and hope you have a  marvellous movie loving week yippie kai  movie lovers
 

